msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:70
msgid "Using Profiles for Optimization (MemPGO)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:72
msgid ""
"Feed the indexed profile back into the compiler using the `-fmemory-profile-"
"use=` option (or low-level passes options)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:78
msgid "If invoking the optimizer directly via `opt`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:84
msgid ""
"The compiler uses the profile data to classify each profiled allocation "
"context based on its average lifetime access density (accesses per byte per "
"lifetime second) and average object lifetime:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:86
msgid ""
"**Cold (`cold`):** Contexts with low lifetime access density (by default, `< "
"0.05` accesses per byte per second) and a sufficiently long average lifetime "
"(by default, at least `200` seconds). Requiring a minimum lifetime avoids "
"placing short-lived allocations onto cold pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:87
msgid ""
"**Hot (`hot`):** Contexts with high lifetime access density (by default, `> "
"1000` accesses per byte per second, when hot hinting is enabled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:88
msgid ""
"**Not Cold (`notcold`):** All other profiled contexts, which are treated as "
"warm by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:90
msgid ""
"Based on this classification, the compiler annotates allocation instructions "
"with `\"memprof\"` attributes (when all contexts reaching a static site "
"agree) or `!memprof` metadata ([MemProf Metadata Documentation]"
"(LangRef.md#memprof-metadata)) to guide downstream optimizations. "
"Additionally, interior callsites that are part of profiled allocation "
"contexts are annotated with `!callsite` metadata ([Callsite Metadata "
"Documentation](LangRef.md#callsite-metadata))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:93
msgid ""
"Ensure that the same debug info flags (e.g. `-gmlt` and `-fdebug-info-for-"
"profiling`) used during instrumentation are also passed during this "
"compilation step to enable correct matching of the profile data. For the "
"optimized binary to fully utilize the hot/cold hinting, it must be linked "
"with an allocator that supports this mechanism, such as [tcmalloc](https://"
"github.com/google/tcmalloc). TCMalloc provides an extended `operator new` "
"API (`__hot_cold_t` / `tcmalloc::hot_cold_t`) that accepts an 8-bit hotness "
"hint (`0` for coldest to `255` for hottest) to guide data placement and "
"improve locality. By default, the compiler passes `1` for `cold`, `128` for "
"`notcold` (warm), `222` for `ambiguous`, and `254` for `hot` allocations "
"(reserving the extremes `0` and `255` for manual hints). To indicate that "
"the allocator library supports these interfaces, the `-mllvm -supports-hot-"
"cold-new` flag is used during the LTO link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:97
msgid "Context Disambiguation (LTO)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:99
msgid ""
"To fully benefit from MemPGO, especially for common allocation wrappers, "
"enabling **ThinLTO** (preferred) or **Full LTO** is required. This allows "
"the compiler to perform **context disambiguation**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:101
msgid "Consider the following example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:117
msgid ""
"Without context disambiguation, the compiler sees a single `allocate` "
"function called from both hot and cold contexts. It must conservatively "
"assume the allocation is \"not cold\" or \"ambiguous\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:119
msgid "With LTO and MemPGO:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:121
msgid "The compiler constructs a whole-program call graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:122
msgid ""
"It identifies that `allocate` has distinct calling contexts with different "
"behaviors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:123
msgid ""
"It **clones** `allocate` into two versions: one for the hot path and one for "
"the cold path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:124
msgid ""
"The call in `cold_path` is updated to call the cloned \"cold\" version of "
"`allocate`, which can then be optimized (e.g., by passing a cold hint to the "
"allocator)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:126
msgid "Static Data Partitioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:128
msgid ""
"MemProf profiles guide the layout of static data (e.g., global variables, "
"constants). The goal is to separate \"hot\" data from \"cold\" data in the "
"binary, placing hot data into specific sections (e.g., `.rodata.hot`) to "
"minimize the number of pages required for the working set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:130
msgid "This feature uses a hybrid approach:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:132
msgid ""
"**Symbolizable Data:** Data with external or local linkage (tracked by the "
"symbol table) is partitioned based on data access profiles collected via "
"instrumentation ([PR](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/142884)) or "
"hardware performance counters (e.g., Intel PEBS events such as "
"`MEM_INST_RETIRED.ALL_LOADS`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:133
msgid ""
"**Module-Internal Data:** Data not tracked by the symbol table (e.g., jump "
"tables, constant pools, internal globals) has its hotness inferred from "
"standard PGO code execution profiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:135
msgid "To enable this feature, pass the following flags to the compiler:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:137
msgid ""
"`-fpartition-static-data-sections`: Instructs the compiler to generate "
"`.hot` and `.unlikely` section prefixes for hot and cold static data "
"respectively in the relocatable object files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:138
msgid ""
"`-Wl,-z,keep-data-section-prefix`: This flag is currently only supported in "
"LLD. It informs the linker that `.data.rel.ro.hot` and "
"`.data.rel.ro.unlikely` are relro sections (rather than only recognizing "
"`.data.rel.ro`). LLD allows multiple relro segments, but not all loaders "
"(particularly glibc) properly support multiple relro segments. This flag "
"ensures a single relro segment to ensure maximum compatibility. "
"Additionally, it makes LLD keep the data section suffixes (hot/unlikely) as "
"otherwise they will get merged together into the standard data sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:144
msgid ""
"The optimized layout clusters hot static data, improving dTLB and cache "
"efficiency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:147
msgid ""
"When both PGO profiles and memory profiles are provided (using `-fprofile-"
"use` and `-fmemory-profile-use`), global variable hotness are inferred from "
"a combination of PGO profile and data access profile:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:151
msgid ""
"For data covered by both profiles (e.g., module-internal data with symbols "
"in the executable), the hotness is the max of PGO profile hotness and data "
"access profile hotness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:154
msgid ""
"For data covered by only one profile, the hotness is inferred from that "
"profile. Most notably, symbolizable data with external linkage is only "
"covered by data access profile, and module-internal unsymbolizable data is "
"only covered by PGO profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:160
msgid "Developer Manual"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:162
msgid ""
"This section provides an overview of the MemPGO architecture and "
"implementation for contributors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:164
msgid "Architecture Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:166
msgid "MemPGO consists of three main components:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:168
msgid ""
"**Instrumentation Pass (Compile-time):** Memory accesses are instrumented to "
"increment the access count held in a shadow memory location, or "
"alternatively to call into the runtime. Memory allocations are intercepted "
"by the runtime library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:169
msgid ""
"**Runtime Library (Link-time/Run-time):** Manages shadow memory and tracks "
"allocation contexts and access statistics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:170
msgid ""
"**Profile Analysis (Post-processing/Compile-time):** Tools and passes that "
"read the profile, annotate the IR using metadata, and perform context "
"disambiguation if necessary when LTO is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:172
msgid "Detailed Workflow (LTO)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:174
msgid ""
"The end-to-end heap optimization pipeline across compile time and LTO "
"involves five stages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:176
msgid ""
"**Profile Matching and Context Trimming:** Using debug information, the "
"profile-use pass maps profiled allocation contexts onto static allocation "
"sites and interior callsites in the IR. All contexts reaching a given static "
"allocation site are organized into a call-stack trie:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:177
msgid ""
"**Unambiguous Sites:** If all contexts reaching the static site share the "
"same classification (or if a configured dominant fraction of allocated bytes "
"is cold), the trie collapses them and attaches a single `\"memprof\"` "
"attribute (`\"cold\"`, `\"notcold\"`, or `\"hot\"`) directly to the "
"allocation call. No call-graph cloning is required for that site."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:178
msgid ""
"**Ambiguous Sites:** If reaching contexts have conflicting classifications "
"(e.g., `cold` from one call path and `notcold` from another), the trie "
"**trims** each call stack to the minimal call-stack prefix required to "
"distinguish its behavior, attaches `!memprof` metadata to the allocation "
"call (along with an `\"ambiguous\"` attribute), and attaches `!callsite` "
"metadata to interior calls along those contexts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:179
msgid ""
"**Summary Serialization (ThinLTO):** During the ThinLTO summary analysis "
"step, the `!memprof` and `!callsite` metadata are serialized into the module "
"summary index so that whole-program context disambiguation can operate "
"directly on the lightweight ThinLTO index without materializing IR across "
"modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:180
msgid ""
"**Whole-Program Calling-Context Graph Construction:** During LTO (either on "
"the IR in Regular LTO or on the combined module summary index during the "
"ThinLTO thin link), the compiler constructs a whole-program calling-context "
"graph for all ambiguous allocations. Nodes represent static allocation sites "
"and interior callsites, while directed caller-to-callee edges carry the "
"trimmed allocation contexts and their target classifications. As the graph "
"is matched against the program's call graph, it accounts for prior inlining "
"(matching multi-frame inline sequences on callsites) and recovers frames "
"elided by tail-call optimization (by searching through direct and indirect "
"tail-call chains)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:181
msgid ""
"**Call-Graph Cloning and Function Assignment:** Starting from each ambiguous "
"allocation node, the disambiguation analysis traverses upward from callees "
"to callers and clones callsite nodes whenever incoming caller edges carry "
"conflicting classifications, partitioning the paths until each cloned "
"allocation node is reached only by a single disambiguated classification. "
"Because a single function may contain multiple cloned callsites, compatible "
"callsite clones within each function are grouped and merged to minimize code "
"duplication before assigning the final set of function clones and rewiring "
"caller edges. In ThinLTO, these cloning and edge-rewiring decisions are "
"recorded in the combined summary index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:182
msgid ""
"**Backend Cloning and Allocator Call Lowering:** In the LTO backend (or "
"directly in Regular LTO), the compiler materializes the assigned function "
"clones, promotes indirect calls where needed to reach cloned callees, "
"rewires call edges to invoke the appropriate clones, and attaches the "
"resolved `\"memprof\"` attribute to each cloned allocation site. Finally, "
"during instruction combining, library call simplification rewrites annotated "
"`operator new` calls (including aligned, `nothrow`, and size-returning "
"variants) to invoke their `__hot_cold_t` overloads with the corresponding 8-"
"bit hotness hint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:184
msgid "Source Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:186
msgid "**Runtime:** `compiler-rt/lib/memprof`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MemPGO.md:188
msgid ""
"Contains the runtime implementation, including shadow memory mapping, "
"interceptors (malloc, free, etc.), and the thread-local storage for "
"recording stats."
msgstr ""

